From: System Electronics
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add the Waveshare DSI panel driver

The Waveshare DSI panels (2.8" to 13.3", including the 10.1" 1280x800 we
use on Astrial H15) are brought up over I2C by an MCU on the adapter
board, the same arrangement the Raspberry Pi 7" panel uses. The driver
for them is not upstream: it lives only in the Raspberry Pi kernel fork,
so linux-yocto-hailo cannot carry it.

Taken from raspberrypi/linux, branch rpi-6.6.y,
drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi.c, and adapted to 5.15:

  - mipi_dsi_device_register_full() / mipi_dsi_attach() instead of the
    devm_ variants, which arrived in 5.19. The unwind they used to do is
    now explicit in the probe error path and in remove().
  - i2c_driver.remove() returns int, the void form landed in 6.1.
  - .probe_new instead of .probe: the single-argument probe signature is
    what .probe_new takes in 5.15.
  - drm_panel_funcs.get_orientation dropped, it appeared in 5.16. The
    orientation still reaches the connector because get_modes() already
    calls drm_connector_set_panel_orientation(), which 5.15 has.

Nothing else was touched. The Kconfig entry sits next to the Raspberry Pi
panel rather than in alphabetical order, because that driver is its
direct ancestor and the two are read together.

Maintenance note: this file has no upstream to track. On a kernel bump it
must be re-taken from the Raspberry Pi fork and re-adapted, and the four
points above are the list to re-check.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [driver is downstream-only in raspberrypi/linux]

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig	2026-09-09 15:29:44.685758095 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig	2026-09-09 15:29:44.705758095 +0200
@@ -341,6 +341,18 @@
 	  Pi 7" Touchscreen.  To compile this driver as a module,
 	  choose M here.
 
+config DRM_PANEL_WAVESHARE_DSI
+	tristate "Waveshare DSI panels"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	help
+	  Say Y here if you want to enable support for the Waveshare
+	  family of DSI panels. The panel is brought up over I2C by an
+	  MCU on the adapter board, the same arrangement the Raspberry
+	  Pi 7" panel uses. To compile this driver as a module, choose
+	  M here.
+
 config DRM_PANEL_RAYDIUM_RM67191
 	tristate "Raydium RM67191 FHD 1080x1920 DSI video mode panel"
 	depends on OF
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile	2026-09-09 15:29:44.695758095 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile	2026-09-09 15:29:44.705758095 +0200
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_OSD_OSD101T2587_53TS) += panel-osd-osd101t2587-53ts.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_PANASONIC_VVX10F034N00) += panel-panasonic-vvx10f034n00.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_RASPBERRYPI_TOUCHSCREEN) += panel-raspberrypi-touchscreen.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_WAVESHARE_DSI) += panel-waveshare-dsi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_RAYDIUM_RM67191) += panel-raydium-rm67191.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_RAYDIUM_RM68200) += panel-raydium-rm68200.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_RONBO_RB070D30) += panel-ronbo-rb070d30.o
